{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic","id":1445855,"title":"Doing away with Prime Magic?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-25T12:20:20-07:00","id":1445855,"title":"Doing away with Prime Magic?","content":"The other day I was listening to Mage: The Podcast. I can't quite remember which episode it was (maybe the one about Action in Mage) bu the guest said something about the lines of &quot;I don't think Prime should even be a Sphere&quot;. That got me thinking.<br /> <br /> Prime Magic never really clicked for me. It's the only Sphere not dealing with something we have IRL, and as such it really feels like a collection of effect rather than a cohesive, living element of the magic System. In the end, Prime magic is mostly dedicated to Quintessence manipulation and little more, besides using it to create something out of nothing. Since Quintessence can be very important mechanically-speaking, most characters end up putting at least 1-2 points in Prime magic as it soon starts feeling not that optional.<br /> <br /> This got me thinking: we already have Avatar as a trait affecting Quintessence manipulation, so would it be possible to delegate quintessence senses, extraction and so on to a simple Avatar roll, while giving the other spheres power to use conjunctional prime magic?<br /> <br /> (loose) examples:<br /> <br /> -Meditating at a node replenishes a number of points of quintessence equal to the successes on an Avatar+Meditation roll<br /> -Extracting from tass requires one success in an Avatar roll<br /> -Sensing the resonance of specific quintessence requires an Avatar+ Awareness roll<br /> <br /> on the other hand, spheres would have intrinsic prime magic<br /> <br /> - imbuing one's fists with Quintessence requires Life 2<br /> - Creating forces out of nothing requires Forces 3<br /> and so on...<br /> <br /> This would obviously make ALL characters more powerful, and can be balanced by removing Avatar from the Background traits and raising its cost in freebie points (even though the balance of it all is not my concern ATM).<br /> <br /> What do you think? Has anyone tried anything similar? Can anyone show me any advantages gameplay-wise in keeping Prime as a Sphere?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26807-nemogg","name":"NemoGG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T12:53:46-07:00","id":1445858,"title":"","content":"Personally I\u2019d get rid of Avatar as a background and use Arete for any mechanics purpose it\u2019s called for while you\u2019re at it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T12:56:12-07:00","id":1445860,"title":"","content":"It certainly would make the creation of Wonders very different. There's also the fact that it deals with <i>finding</i> and <i>maintaining</i> Nodes. <br /> <br /> Bear in mind that Prime is the Sphere most suited to the notion of geomancy, or feng shui, along with similar notions such as sacred geometry. It's not just about Quintessence, although there's much for it to do even dealing just with that; it also deals with Resonance and Synergy. In fact, feng shui could be described as the art of manipulating the Synergy of an area. <br /> <br /> If anything, the problem here isn't that Prime doesn't correspond to anything \u201creal\u201d (in the sense of real world beliefs); it's that the likes of Resonance and Synergy are too restricted to Magick-only. There are professional feng shui experts in China whose jobs are to arrange things so that a domicile has \u201cgood vibes\u201d in it and will enhance the lives of the denizens therein. In effect, setting up the local Synergy to impart advantages. This could be modeled quite effectively by allowing synergy from such places to affect more than just magic that's cast there.<br /> <br /> Rather than removing Prime, if you don't think it's effective enough then make it more effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T12:58:12-07:00","id":1445861,"title":"","content":"Tentatively, I'm not a huge fan of the idea. Aside from the fact that there are other Spheres dealing with things that don't exist IRL (AFAIK, Spirit isn't a tangible thing here), I think you're forgetting that even if all the Spheres minus Prime cover things that exist in our world, there is obviously one thing that doesn't exist in ours: Magic (again, AFAIK). Prime is the &quot;meta-magic&quot; Sphere, the Sphere about Magic that affects Other Magic. I think it makes sense to have that as a Sphere as anything else, arguably more. And I think trying to move every feature of the Prime Sphere into another Sphere or the Avatar Trait seems like it creates more trouble than it's worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T13:15:33-07:00","id":1445863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445861#post1445861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tentatively, I'm not a huge fan of the idea. Aside from the fact that there are other Spheres dealing with things that don't exist IRL (AFAIK, Spirit isn't a tangible thing here), I think you're forgetting that even if all the Spheres minus Prime cover things that exist in our world, there is obviously one thing that doesn't exist in ours: Magic (again, AFAIK). Prime is the &quot;meta-magic&quot; Sphere, the Sphere about Magic that affects Other Magic. I think it makes sense to have that as a Sphere as anything else, arguably more. And I think trying to move every feature of the Prime Sphere into another Sphere or the Avatar Trait seems like it creates more trouble than it's worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>there\u2019s just so much of that that should be inherent powers of being a Mage rather than needing a specific sphere for, or where it\u2019s a tax on doing things that should be covered by other spheres (the ubiquitous requirement for Prime 2)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T13:59:39-07:00","id":1445866,"title":"","content":"To demonstrate an issue with Prime RAW - have you noticed how every group that specializes in making Wonders (other than fetishes) tend toward specializing in Matter? None of them specialize in Prime despite in the actual rules that being the integral sphere to their Modus Operandi. Like shouldn\u2019t ItX and the Etherites and House Verditius all be heavily Prime specialized RAW.<br /> <br /> How would the balance of the game change if Matter was the integral sphere for imbuing Wonders with power? Or alternatively what if all you need are the spheres of the effects you are imbueing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T14:07:24-07:00","id":1445867,"title":"","content":"I've made a new magic system for the same reasons. I didn't like the entropy sphere, and wanted to rethink coincidental magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11911-corey","name":"Corey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11911_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T14:29:17-07:00","id":1445871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445866#post1445866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To demonstrate an issue with Prime RAW - have you noticed how every group that specializes in making Wonders (other than fetishes) tend toward specializing in Matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I haven't. The Syndicate doesn't specialize in Matter, but it's the primary source of Wonders in the Technocracy \u2014 largely because it <i>does</i> specialize in Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T14:35:13-07:00","id":1445873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445863#post1445863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> there\u2019s just so much of that that should be inherent powers of being a Mage rather than needing a specific sphere for, or where it\u2019s a tax on doing things that should be covered by other spheres (the ubiquitous requirement for Prime 2)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445858#post1445858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I\u2019d get rid of Avatar as a background and use Arete for any mechanics purpose it\u2019s called for while you\u2019re at it</div> </div> </div> </div>that's a GREAT idea. I understand the different narrative purpose of the two, but it really would feel much more cohesive as a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26807-nemogg","name":"NemoGG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T14:41:39-07:00","id":1445874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445860#post1445860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It certainly would make the creation of Wonders very different. There's also the fact that it deals with <i>finding</i> and <i>maintaining</i> Nodes.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind that Prime is the Sphere most suited to the notion of geomancy, or feng shui, along with similar notions such as sacred geometry. It's not just about Quintessence, although there's much for it to do even dealing just with that; it also deals with Resonance and Synergy. In fact, feng shui could be described as the art of manipulating the Synergy of an area.<br /> <br /> If anything, the problem here isn't that Prime doesn't correspond to anything \u201creal\u201d (in the sense of real world beliefs); it's that the likes of Resonance and Synergy are too restricted to Magick-only. There are professional feng shui experts in China whose jobs are to arrange things so that a domicile has \u201cgood vibes\u201d in it and will enhance the lives of the denizens therein. In effect, setting up the local Synergy to impart advantages. This could be modeled quite effectively by allowing synergy from such places to affect more than just magic that's cast there.<br /> <br /> Rather than removing Prime, if you don't think it's effective enough then make it more effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>this is actually very interesting, and making it so Prime deals with Resonance and the like actually feels very flavorful, I must say. It does run into the same problems I was alluding to in the original post tho.<br /> <br /> To rephrase the matter, it seems to me that Prime is the only sphere that comes with a set number of effects, kind of like a spell list \u00e0 la D&amp;D if you will. Of course it's the Metamagic Sphere, i get that, but it really feels... artificial (for lack of a better term) to play.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26807-nemogg","name":"NemoGG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T15:11:30-07:00","id":1445877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445871#post1445871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I haven't. The Syndicate doesn't specialize in Matter, but it's the primary source of Wonders in the Technocracy \u2014 largely because it <i>does</i> specialize in Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they\u2019re not. Iteration X are the primary makers of devices (followed by Q Division internally to the NWO). Physical tech is their whole thing. The Syndicate had a barrabi faction that made Bane Fetishes (using spirit), but those were their only dedicated Device crafters, and are very dead now.<br /> <br /> why would you go to a bunch of economists, bankers, and venture capitalists to do the work of physically making you tech instead of the mechanical engineers!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-25-2021, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T15:28:31-07:00","id":1445880,"title":"","content":"There's a reason one of the Instruments used by the Syndicate is Management and Human Resources \u2014<br /> or, as it's phrased in the Syndicate Convention Book, Personnel. You're right that the Syndics don't get their <i>own</i> hands dirty making Wonders; but it's <i>their</i> assembly lines and the workers on said lines that do the building. Where Iteration X comes in is the innovating: creating, and then perfecting, the prototypes. But after that, is off to the Syndicate's mass production facilities to churn out as many of those things as the Syndicate has the supplies to produce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T15:52:55-07:00","id":1445886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445863#post1445863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there\u2019s just so much of that that should be inherent powers of being a Mage rather than needing a specific sphere for, or where it\u2019s a tax on doing things that should be covered by other spheres (the ubiquitous requirement for Prime 2)</div> </div> </div> </div>I hesitated to post initially because I am sympathetic to the position to some degree. I can see the argument for having the &quot;magic-magic&quot; being a set of universal powers that all Mages possess. I can also see where having Prime as the &quot;meta-magic Sphere&quot; might run a bit of a risk of being seen as an uber-Sphere (thought Spirit actually seems to end up being that more in practice). I think the most sympathy I have for the argument of removing the Prime Sphere is that I personally consider it completely indispensable in any Mage character-concept I've put together; but even that seems more like a matter of personal taste than a pragmatic min-max decision.<br /> <br /> To me, it just makes sense that there would be a &quot;field of study&quot; regarding the 'mechanics' of True Magic to the same extent that other Spheres are treated as distinctive bodies of knowledge. And I think folding most of those various abilities and Effects into the Arete or Avatar Traits removes too much of the distinction between &quot;knowledge/skill&quot; and &quot;power level.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T19:16:36-07:00","id":1445904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445880#post1445880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason one of the Instruments used by the Syndicate is Management and Human Resources \u2014<br /> or, as it's phrased in the Syndicate Convention Book, Personnel. You're right that the Syndics don't get their <i>own</i> hands dirty making Wonders; but it's <i>their</i> assembly lines and the workers on said lines that do the building. Where Iteration X comes in is the innovating: creating, and then perfecting, the prototypes. But after that, is off to the Syndicate's mass production facilities to churn out as many of those things as the Syndicate has the supplies to produce.</div> </div> </div> </div>So doe It X scientists not need Prime to create Devices provided they\u2019ve got a Prime Utility wielding Syndicate rep invested in the project?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T20:04:54-07:00","id":1445910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NemoGG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445874#post1445874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To rephrase the matter, it seems to me that Prime is the only sphere that comes with a set number of effects, kind of like a spell list \u00e0 la D&amp;D if you will. Of course it's the Metamagic Sphere, i get that, but it really feels... artificial (for lack of a better term) to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think that's the case. Prime, at least in Revised, comes with A LOT of flavor text that poetizes every bit as much about what that Sphere does as Forces or Spirit - after that, dynamic magick it's just ST creativity and realizing the book doesn't always have all the answers<br /> <br /> While you can &quot;fold&quot; a what Prime does in other Spheres and Avatar/Arete, the same can be said of <i>any </i>Sphere. And in the case of Prime it will end feeling very artificial because there are things that just can't be tought w/o the <i>concepts</i> of Prime<br /> <br /> For instance, I can &quot;atomize&quot; someone with Forces, a lo Prime 5 - but can I redirect the free Quintessence that was released to power another spell with <i>Forces</i>?. Or now Avatar does that each time you kill someone?<br /> <br /> If magick resistance its a fucnction of Avatar: How can I use Matter to make armor that resist magick (Primium)?, or a plant that absorbs and concentrates Quintessence for future consumption (soulflower). Do I need to raise Avatar to make Primium and Soulflowers?<br /> <br /> OK. Now I want to create a flame that <i>damages magick</i>, also I want my dog to <i>smell Paradox</i>.<br /> <br /> I really think that Prime isn't any less dynamic than most other Spheres. And, at the risk of being pretentious, I really believe that;<br /> <br /> A)The observed problems are subjective: I've observed that those players with a background or hard sciences tend to use Pattern Spheres with a lot more creativity and power, and don't know what to do with Entropy, Prime and Spirit. Meanwhile, players with a background on literature or mysticism tend to use those last three with a lot more creativity, and don't know what to do with, say Matter (I once ranked that Sphere as the least useful, because I didn't understood well how to use it - now my opinion has changed because I know more, and thus what I can imagine doing changed)<br /> <br /> B)A lot of the problems with &quot;Spheres that don't relate to the real world&quot; can be solved by thinking about what this &quot;methaphisical&quot; statement says about the world<br /> <br /> Ultimately, objects &quot;that don't relate to the real world&quot; - and I mean ALL of them (Spirits, Ephemera, the Soul, the shadows of Obtenebration, the Curse of Caine, Faes, Paradox, Magick...) - are just objects that the ST needs to rule.<br /> <br /> And really, that's no different from Time or Life. Sure, you may think that the ST may not have to &quot;invent&quot; what the body does when manipulated in a certain way with Life because there's SCIENCE to explain what happens...but in truth most ST's haven't a PhD in Biology, and thus are liable to &quot;enact&quot; all kinds of misconceptions about the limits and powers of Life.<br /> So, in the end, the ST does &quot;invent&quot; what biology &quot;realistically&quot; does, too - it's just less of an obvious sham, if you don't have a player that knows about the subject<br /> <br /> I don't think Prime would become useless if you decoupled Wonders and Creation from it. It would become less mandatory,but at the same time it could be a good time to explore a litttle more some of the implications of meta-magick existing (allowing it to actualy alter some of the <i>other </i>rules of magick, w/o fearing that Prime would end as even more of a &quot;must have&quot; that it already is).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">But I don't think that you *should* decouple Wonders from Prime, because Wonders are &quot;objects with magick&quot; - it makes A LOT of sense to use the sphere of magick to proivide magick to that which hasn't it.<br /> <br /> A better solution for crafters it's to take a page from Revised, and make ALL Wonders require one level less to create if you use Tass ressonant with the desired effects. Bonus points because it's more aesthetical to see mages craft their hellfire Wonders with the bones of hellhounds, than just grabbing whatever Quintessence they have in the house to make 'em...the Syndicate it's more efficient, but it's the efficiency of </span>boredom<span style=\"font-size:14px\">.<br /> <br /> Creation and Prime </span>were strongly related in the old lore, albeit it's less obvious now. The relation of Prime/Magick with The One and the Pures, I think it's the main justification behind the Chorus having it as primary Sphere - but this ... I can see <i>this </i>being decoupled and added to the other Spheres simply to avoid the hussle of &quot;having&quot; to get Prime 2 just to do a damn fireball.<br /> <br /> Prime should be for those mages that want to study <i>the stuff of magick itself</i> (Quintessence, Paradox, Mages...), not a tax on D&amp;D stile magick...but at the same time I'm a bit fond of the old lore of Prime = &quot;the spark of Creation itself&quot;, and all that it implies. So I would like to preserve that lore somehow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-25-2021, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T04:10:29-07:00","id":1445948,"title":"","content":"I don't think Prime getting axed is the right move.<br /> <br /> If you're trying to figure out how to expand Prime a bit from just being the Sphere that governs magic, you could look at Awakening 2e for some inspirations of effects to put under Prime (and Awakening took out the Prime 2 for empowering other Arcana thing, made magical senses standard mage powers, and has plenty of ways to gain Mana without Prime or even spells). Two of the big things Prime governs in Awakening besides magic are purity and truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T04:42:07-07:00","id":1445954,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Awakening replaced the Prime 2 requirement with a Mastery retirement. <br /> <br /> I could see retooling Forces to allow for <i>ex nihilo</i> creation of lightning, flame, light, and so on, maybe at one more dot than it's needed to manipulate them; but I prefer that Life and Matter stick to requiring some sort of conjunctive effect for the creation or destruction of their patterns. It doesn't necessarily have to be Prime; though I can see the case for that being the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T05:07:03-07:00","id":1445958,"title":"","content":"You don't need Mastery to fireball someone in Awakening. But the point is that what you can do in Awakening is far less likely to have Prime 2 tacked on to &quot;fuel&quot; it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T06:43:15-07:00","id":1445964,"title":"","content":"In my extensive pre-M20 house rules, I split primes fuel effect and break down into quintessence off into their respective spheres and gave the rest (prime body, making weapons deal agg, etc) to Spirit (and refined Spirit as specifically dealing with the Middle Umbra while Mind acts like Spirit for the High Umbra and Death -see below- interacted with the Low Umbra). <br /> <br /> Then to keeps the number at nine I added Death and moved a lot of the conjunctional effects (ex. Animate Dead is Matter/Prime in HDYDT? Going to the Low Umbra was Spirit/Entropy) into it (I had a PC Necromancer at the time and the fact that just about everything required lots of high level conjunctional effects with far more non-necromancy uses encouraged me to split off Death into its own sphere).<br /> <br /> The Mind/Spirit/Death split also helped put greater focus on distinctions in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> I dunno if I do that again in M20, but that\u2019s more because my interests for magic have evolved more towards something like DA\u2019s foundations and pillars approach that deals less with \u201cwhat\u2019s the nature of reality/how does everything fit together?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T07:55:52-07:00","id":1445970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445964#post1445964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my extensive pre-M20 house rules, I split primes fuel effect and break down into quintessence off into their respective spheres and gave the rest (prime body, making weapons deal agg, etc) to Spirit (and refined Spirit as specifically dealing with the Middle Umbra while Mind acts like Spirit for the High Umbra and Death -see below- interacted with the Low Umbra).<br /> <br /> Then to keeps the number at nine I added Death and moved a lot of the conjunctional effects (ex. Animate Dead is Matter/Prime in HDYDT? Going to the Low Umbra was Spirit/Entropy) into it (I had a PC Necromancer at the time and the fact that just about everything required lots of high level conjunctional effects with far more non-necromancy uses encouraged me to split off Death into its own sphere).<br /> <br /> The Mind/Spirit/Death split also helped put greater focus on distinctions in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> I dunno if I do that again in M20, but that\u2019s more because my interests for magic have evolved more towards something like DA\u2019s foundations and pillars approach that deals less with \u201cwhat\u2019s the nature of reality/how does everything fit together?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly the kind of experience I was looking to read about. How did the game flow? Was it too powerful giving Prime effect &quot;for free&quot; to the other spheres? Did it take away from the metaphysics and the &quot;fluff&quot;debates?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26807-nemogg","name":"NemoGG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T08:01:33-07:00","id":1445971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445948#post1445948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Prime getting axed is the right move.<br /> <br /> If you're trying to figure out how to expand Prime a bit from just being the Sphere that governs magic, you could look at Awakening 2e for some inspirations of effects to put under Prime (and Awakening took out the Prime 2 for empowering other Arcana thing, made magical senses standard mage powers, and has plenty of ways to gain Mana without Prime or even spells). Two of the big things Prime governs in Awakening besides magic are purity and truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting, I only have Revised as sourcebook, so I never came across this interpretation, and Truth (as in seeing things how they really are) looks like something that is actually missing from the Revised spheres. Would you say it can be used to do Hieromancy (&quot;law magic&quot;)? As in, establishing a particular set of laws, nudging the local consensus in a specific direction among other things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26807-nemogg","name":"NemoGG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T08:57:35-07:00","id":1445978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NemoGG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445970#post1445970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is exactly the kind of experience I was looking to read about. How did the game flow? Was it too powerful giving Prime effect &amp;quot;for free&amp;quot; to the other spheres? Did it take away from the metaphysics and the &amp;quot;fluff&amp;quot;debates?</div> </div> </div> </div>It flowed very well and actually seemed to help the metaphysics, honestly. The fact that with adept rank you could pull in quintessence from the cosmos to create a thing and with mastery in a sphere you understood it sufficiently to break it down... and that by linking it to spheres made the idea of, for example, using mastery of Mind to dissolve a mental concept into raw quintessence... I felt reinforced the idea that reality was composed of quintessence patterns and that mastery of a given sphere allowed you to manipulate those patterns directly. The capstone that really sold it though was the rank 5 prime effect of creating a node, because with it distributed among the spheres it allowed mages to concentrate the aspects of their mastery into nodes with more character and resonance... a Forces node was not a Mind node was not a Death node.<br /> <br /> This also played into my meta-setting\u2019s (I\u2019ve run a virtually continuous Mage campaign in the same ongoing setting for 25 years now) focus on Anchorheads; expanded from generic thin spots to the Umbra into nine mega-nodes (one for each sphere) that anchor reality and that slowly shift position based on where humanity most associates that sphere (ex; the anchorhead of Forces was located in the Ubar Fields in Saudi Arabia... the largest source of oil in the world) and the war between the Technocracy and Tradition masters over their control (some go missing for a time as the consensus changed over the years and a race to claim it is on) since it\u2019s believed that controlling the majority of them swings the nature of the world in your direction.<br /> <br /> Anyway, in my experience, Prime was largely a \u201cfeat tax\u201d; something you had to put dots into if your magic concept worked with Forces, Life or Matter to get the same sort of results that one would expect from Entropy or Mind or Spirit or Time without any such conjunctions needed.<br /> <br /> Basically, everyone either got two dots in prime to store quintessence/generic counter-magick/fuel patterns/deal agg and then forgot Prime existed because it was only ever used as a conjunctional add-on or to refill the \u201cmana bar\u201d -or- the occasional PC who wanted to craft items and/or pattern rip would go all the way to 5 dots as a hyper specialist.<br /> <br /> The last thing you want in a system is a \u201cfeat tax.\u201d It\u2019s just a speed bump applied to certain abilities for reasons (i.e. \u201cno, you don\u2019t get the cool toy X you were expecting, first you have to unlock Y to use X\u2019s full power\u201d).<br /> <br /> Besides, once M20 clarified you can fly or use telekinesis with Forces 2 by redirecting gravity it also became really obvious you could just use the transmute level to defacto fuel Forces patterns by transmuting gravity or ambient light into heat or lightning and defacto fuel Matter patterns by transmuting the air or the upper molecules of every nearby surface, etc.<br /> <br /> The result being that all adding the Prime elements to the spheres really did was simplify the explanations; instead of converting gravity to heat, you just create heat; instead of converting air to steel you just create the steel.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I mostly found that dropping Prime just meant that item creation, vulgar pattern rips and node creation weren\u2019t locked up behind one specialist who could pretty much only do those terribly specific things, but instead available in limited ways to everyone... the master of Mind could create talismans related to mind magic, the Forces master could make staves that channel lightning, the Life mage could brew healing tonics (or viscous poisons), etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T15:02:15-07:00","id":1445995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NemoGG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445971#post1445971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is interesting, I only have Revised as sourcebook, so I never came across this interpretation, and Truth (as in seeing things how they really are) looks like something that is actually missing from the Revised spheres. Would you say it can be used to do Hieromancy (&quot;law magic&quot;)? As in, establishing a particular set of laws, nudging the local consensus in a specific direction among other things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening is a different game/setting with different assumptions, so direct transfer from it to Ascension is always going to be a bit clunky.<br /> <br /> Awakening doesn't deal with consensual reality, so hieromancy like that isn't directly in their examples of how to use Prime to express using truth as a form of magic, but there's no reason you couldn't. One of the example Prime spells in Awakening 2e lets you speak Truth, that is, express something you strongly feel is true with such power behind it that the Truth behind your statement is so powerful everyone that can hear you knows what you're saying; ignoring things like language barriers.<br /> <br /> If you added that sort of effect to Ascension's take on Prime, you could definitely build it up as part of pushing local Reality around. It also makes the Chorus as the Tradition holding the Seat of Prime make a lot more sense since that sort of soulful expression that transcends human boundaries would totally be something that would make Prime a major focus for them.<br /> <br /> Another example that mixes the Magic and Truth themes of Prime in Awakening 2e is a spell that lets you circumvent attempts to encode magical items (not just mage made ones either) with specific actions, phrases, or whatever to make the magic in them happen. By commanding a wand of fireballs to express its Truth (it shoots fireballs), Prime can get around pesky things like having to intone a Latin phrase to get it to work.<br /> <br /> This sort of &quot;reveal magic for what it truly is&quot; sort of effect could be a very interesting part of Ascension. The Technocrats trying to &quot;debunk&quot; mystic Reality Zones by revealing the Truth of a spell is not the mystic trappings the Traditions use and that Sleepers start to believe in, and the Traditions causing Union hardware to go nuts as the veneer of technological plausibility gets broken by revealing the true nature of their devices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T20:54:56-07:00","id":1446408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1445995#post1445995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awakening is a different game/setting with different assumptions, so direct transfer from it to Ascension is always going to be a bit clunky.<br /> <br /> Awakening doesn't deal with consensual reality, so hieromancy like that isn't directly in their examples of how to use Prime to express using truth as a form of magic, but there's no reason you couldn't. One of the example Prime spells in Awakening 2e lets you speak Truth, that is, express something you strongly feel is true with such power behind it that the Truth behind your statement is so powerful everyone that can hear you knows what you're saying; ignoring things like language barriers.<br /> <br /> If you added that sort of effect to Ascension's take on Prime, you could definitely build it up as part of pushing local Reality around. It also makes the Chorus as the Tradition holding the Seat of Prime make a lot more sense since that sort of soulful expression that transcends human boundaries would totally be something that would make Prime a major focus for them.<br /> <br /> Another example that mixes the Magic and Truth themes of Prime in Awakening 2e is a spell that lets you circumvent attempts to encode magical items (not just mage made ones either) with specific actions, phrases, or whatever to make the magic in them happen. By commanding a wand of fireballs to express its Truth (it shoots fireballs), Prime can get around pesky things like having to intone a Latin phrase to get it to work.<br /> <br /> This sort of &quot;reveal magic for what it truly is&quot; sort of effect could be a very interesting part of Ascension. The Technocrats trying to &quot;debunk&quot; mystic Reality Zones by revealing the Truth of a spell is not the mystic trappings the Traditions use and that Sleepers start to believe in, and the Traditions causing Union hardware to go nuts as the veneer of technological plausibility gets broken by revealing the true nature of their devices.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last paragraph sort of illustrates why applying this &quot;Truth&quot; aspect to Ascension is fraught with complications. While Awakening is all about exposing a single hidden Truth, Ascension is all about everyone's &quot;Truth&quot; being equally valid. Which is to say, any mage doing this sort of thing is doing the metaphysical equivalent of saying &quot;nuh uh!&quot; to another mage's magick or tools.<br /> <br /> Although in that sense, Ascension's version of Prime already has that. It's called Countermagic/Antimagic/Unweaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T23:28:07-07:00","id":1446418,"title":"","content":"Complications aren't necessarily bad things though. Plus Awakening isn't actually about exposing a single hidden truth, but stripping away lies. The Supernal is not one Truth, but a plethora of Truths.<br /> <br /> And my example as well about &quot;nuh-uh&quot; on other mages' magic, but rather about eliminating that trappings in the eyes of those perceiving the magic. It wouldn't inherently counter a spell, but would be able to influence vulgarity, or trigger effects at inconvenient times. This plays into trying to play with the edges of Reality Zones.<br /> <br /> Counter/anti-magic is about negating the truth magic expresses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T09:28:20-07:00","id":1446451,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: is not so much about everything being equally true as it is that the question of \u201cwhat is true?\u201d isn't so easily answered as casting a spell. There are some things that are definitely true no matter what you personally believe; for insurance, Avatars exist. But what, specifically, an Avatar is, beyond \u201cwhatever it is that empowers Mages\u201d,9 is open to debate, and is not the sort of thing that can be established through a Prime Effect.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I could definitely see Prime's repertoire being expanded to include \u201cillusions\u201d \u2014 which I put in quotes because it's not about deception. You can do the \u201cdeception of the senses\u201d thing with Forces. What the Prime version would be like would be more along the lines of Glamour: think of it as step one for creating something out of the Pattern Spheres, but without the Pattern Spheres. The downside would be that such Prime patterns would be susceptible to countermagick and Unbelief; the upside would be that you could do more with less: \u201cillusions\u201d of things wouldn't require as many successes to create as the things themselves. <br /> <br /> My own gut instinct would be to make this sort of thing conjunctional magic, assort of inversion of the usual rule about needing two dots of Prime to create things with the Pattern spheres: instead, you might need two dots of, say, Forces to create an \u201cillusion\u201d of fire using Prime. But that's just me: personally, I prefer that all of the tangible effects of Prime involve some sort of conjunctional use with an appropriate Pattern sphere. But then, I get plenty of use out of the intangible applications of Prime.<br /> <br /> And in a similar vein, I've got a hack (check the classical world of Darkness section in my sig) for spell books: a sort of hybrid between a grimoire and an artifact for talisman that lets Mages cast wrote that they don't have the appropriate Spheres for. In conjunction with the aforementioned sorcerer the paths of power, I would praise him in terms of granting access to the sorceress Rote Merit So long as you have the spellbook handy, and to aid in acquiring said Merit through study. The relevance to Prime is that you need it in order to create a spell book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-29-2021, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T10:15:34-07:00","id":1446455,"title":"","content":"I like Heavy Arms idea - just not so much the whole &quot;Truth&quot; thing, but I don't think it's necessary to delve so hard on that part<br /> <br /> For instance: &quot;By commanding a wand of fireballs to express its Truth (it shoots fireballs), Prime can get around pesky things like having to intone a Latin phrase to get it to work.&quot;<br /> <br /> I could easily frame that as Prime <i>commanding </i>the magick/psionics/&quot;however your mage likes to call what mages of diferent Focuses do, and that Prime normaly allows to counter&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't need to frame it as &quot;truth-mancy&quot;, albeit some mages definitely could - it's just &quot;hacking&quot; an artifact, bypassing certain restrictions. Prime creates artifacts, and sometimes repair artifacts...Now it commands artifacts (instead, or on top of that)<br /> <br /> &quot;influence vulgarity, or trigger effects at inconvenient times&quot;, in the same vein, don't need to be frame as The Truth(tm) existing. It's just controling stuff that's already related to magick<br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow Prime to detect the truth of <i>statements</i>, Entropy already does that, and in a way it makes more sense with Ascencion...but revealing the &quot;truths&quot; of the supernatural world, Prime already kinda does that with it's &quot;detect magick&quot; functions, I see the rest as largely an extension of that (that does risk, in my opinion, making Prime too powerful- but could compensate &quot;taking away&quot; from Prime the stuff one thinks all mages should be able to do by default)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-29-2021, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T10:15:55-07:00","id":1446456,"title":"","content":"On the notion of using Prime to manipulate \u201ctruth\u201d, as Heavy Arms is suggesting, I'd like to point out that <b>Sorcerer: Paths of Power</b> has a section in it that adapts the Wonder creation rules to allow mages to use Prime to create a Sorcerous Path. Mind you, while I like the principle behind it, I tend to think that it makes the creation of sorceress paths a little too easy. But I do like the principle of it. It's the sort of thing that I could see a master of prime doing, though even there I would put the requirements more extreme than the ones that are needed to craft Wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T10:25:18-07:00","id":1446457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1446455#post1446455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Heavy Arms idea - just not so much the whole &quot;Truth&quot; thing, but I don't think it's necessary to delve so hard on that part<br /> <br /> For instance: &quot;By commanding a wand of fireballs to express its Truth (it shoots fireballs), Prime can get around pesky things like having to intone a Latin phrase to get it to work.&quot;<br /> <br /> I could easily frame that as Prime <i>commanding </i>the magick/psionics/&quot;however your mage likes to call what mages of diferent Focuses do, and that Prime normaly allows to counter&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't need to frame it as &quot;truth-mancy&quot;, albeit some mages definitely could - it's just &quot;hacking&quot; an artifact, bypassing certain restrictions. Prime creates artifacts, and sometimes repair artifacts...Now it commands artifacts (instead, or on top of that)<br /> <br /> &quot;influence vulgarity, or trigger effects at inconvenient times&quot;, in the same vein, don't need to be frame as The Truth(tm) existing. It's just controling stuff that's already related to magick<br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow Prime to detect the truth of <i>statements</i>, Entropy already does that, and in a way it makes more sense with Ascencion...but revealing the &quot;truths&quot; of the supernatural world, Prime already kinda does that with it's &quot;detect magick&quot; functions, I see the rest as largely an extension of that (that does risk, in my opinion, making Prime too powerful- but could compensate &quot;taking away&quot; from Prime the stuff one thinks all mages should be able to do by default)</div> </div> </div> </div>The ability to spend quintessence to neutralize paradox kind of falls into this territory as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T11:13:47-07:00","id":1446462,"title":"","content":"Well, the reason I'm stressing Prime as Truth is more of giving Prime additional flavor so it feels less like the&quot;meta-magic&quot; Sphere; as is the original complaint about it in the thread.<br /> <br /> This idea doesn't need to be about the setting have a single overriding Truth above all others. Awakening doesn't even have that thanks to Archmages mucking around in the Supernal.<br /> <br /> In this case it's more &quot;revealing things for what they are.&quot; It's not a violation of Ascension's metaphysics or themes for the idea of revealing the truth to include letting people see what a stage magician is actually doing instead of being caught up in the show. Ascension frequently points out that Sleepers confuse the tools for the magic; something that is essential for mages to work coincidental magic in unfriendly Reality Zones because they can adjust their tools to disguise what they're really doing.<br /> <br /> As well, the &quot;lie detector&quot; effect from Awakening is easy to work into Ascension while maintaining Ascension's themes: it's detecting reality vs. the target's ideal Pattern. There's a reason the Awakening &quot;lie detector&quot; spell can't detect serial liars like Mind can, but can spot someone that's using hair dye, or a falsified form: the reality of a thing is in contradiction with the Pattern of the thing, even if in a small enough way to not have major metaphysical consequences.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T12:11:25-07:00","id":1446473,"title":"","content":"As has already been pointed out, Ascension already has a light detector effect: it's under entropy, and I'm low to take anything away from entropy considering that I view it to be in need of some buttressing as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T12:28:15-07:00","id":1446475,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea of Prime as Truth, since multiple competing truths doesn't bother me for MtAsc. <br /> <br /> The stage magician example is a tricky one, though. What does it mean to inject truth in In stage magic? It shouldn't just be directing attention to the actual motions, that's more of a Mind thing. It should probably manifest as more of a awareness of the existence of the false narrative and an unwillingness to go along with it. The audience doesn't actually see the trick any better, they just find it less convincing. If that is the case, though, then I would suggest not using stage magic as the example, because in stage magic the truth is often already a part of the act. The audience often knows they are being fooled and are there for the enjoyment. <br /> <br /> Perhaps using the convoluted cons of shows like Hustle and Leverage would be a better example. Injecting truth into the con might make it more real and more plausible. Pulling truth out of it or injecting it into the world makes it less convincing. What is reinforced or eroded in this case is the narrative. Essentially the spell creates a temporary Mythic Thread that either works for or against the endeavor.<br /> <br /> This does seem like a paradigmatic interpretation of Prime rather than the Sphere itself, though, so perhaps there's a better way of expressing the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T12:35:01-07:00","id":1446476,"title":"","content":"Mind can detect lies too... Mage (either) is full of multiple ways to pull off similar but too close to be different mechanically effects with different Spheres. You could argue that since Prime is also capable of Aura reading, that lie detection would already be something it can do as an extended function of that. <br /> <br /> I'd also wager that very few people think Entropy is at risk of doing little (esp. once Entropy 4 comes into play). Ring of Truth is one of the many little Entropy effects that is rather tangential to the core themes of the Sphere (though not wrong for being there by any means) that gives Entropy a reputation for being a grab-bag that can do anything if you have enough dots/get creative. A lot of people have thought about copying Awakening's removal of Entropy to get Fate and Death...which doesn't really imply Entropy does too much too that group at a minimum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T12:40:31-07:00","id":1446477,"title":"","content":"The stage magician example is less about what the spell would do in Ascension, and more about how Ascension treats the divide between tools and effects; esp. regarding hiding your magic under the cloak of what the local Reality Zone finds acceptable. Being a stage magician is how mages fool the HAP of Consensus, or reinforce Sleeper perceptions that create Reality Zones, and Prime would have the ability to interact with that process.<br /> <br /> In application, such a spell would absolutely be more like creating temporary mythic threads (or suppressing existing ones) and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T05:12:03-07:00","id":1446586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1446476#post1446476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind can detect lies too... Mage (either) is full of multiple ways to pull off similar but too close to be different mechanically effects with different Spheres. You could argue that since Prime is also capable of Aura reading, that lie detection would already be something it can do as an extended function of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. My issue was only that the method should be subtly different if possible. Detecting aura vs detecting intent vs detecting discrepancy. That kind of thing. In this case reinforcing the actual believability of the act vs increasing or decreasing a person's feelings about the act.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445855-doing-away-with-prime-magic?p=1446477#post1446477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In application, such a spell would absolutely be more like creating temporary mythic threads (or suppressing existing ones) and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like we are very much on the same page then.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T06:45:06-07:00","id":1446593,"title":"","content":"Or set up a (temporary or permanent) Sanctum. They exist, and they don't come into being spontaneously; so someone had to make them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T18:29:34-07:00","id":1447316,"title":"","content":"Great post and interesting responses! To touch back on NemoGG's initial question...<br /> <br /> I would not like to see Prime deleted from the game. It figures into an awful lot of underlying metaphysics that would get complicated to explain without it. However, if I am reading the post correctly, it is not the concept of Prime that is the problem, but rather the mechanics associated with it, i.e. being a point sink to do the things you really want to with Pattern magic with no seemingly inherent value on its own.<br /> <br /> While I could argue for all the really cool uses for Prime, instead I will suggest linking Prime to Arete and just making a house rule that for every point of Arete, the characters get a point of Prime. This fulfills the Pattern magic itch - you cannot fireball without Forces 2 or 3 anyway and it streamlines the play to focus on what your groups think is fun, which is the overall point of the game, without breaking or even altering the fundamental mechanics of the game.<br /> <br /> This can be explained that since Quintessence is the underlying source of all reality, understanding in Prime is a metaphysical aspect of enlightenment attained with Arete, not a discipline to study by rote. In this case, a mage does not learn Prime, they grow to understand it as they grow to understand magic as a whole and grow in Arete.<br /> <br /> This of course brings up the issue of what to do with all those points, if the mage gets this huge freebie? My answer to that is push Skills. If Arete is personal growth and understanding of Prime is a part of that deep understanding, it separates it from the other spheres. The logic follows that these other spheres are learned and need to be studied to be used.<br /> <br /> This gives a mechanical use for rotes and for paradigm because Sphere effects learned and rely on a suite of knowledge skills to use properly. If a Hermetic mage wants to throw a fireball, it is no longer just Forces 2 or 3 and Prime. Now it requires an answer to this question: &quot;does the mage know how to create a fireball? Yeah? How do they do it?&quot; Fueling fire with Prime is all good, but where does that Prime come from and how does the mage harness it? A Hermetic could evoke the name of Marduk, or a primal celestial of flame, or Sol Invictus. However, in the Hermetic paradigm, all things are connected and sympathetic to each other. Is today a day that Sol Invictus is listening? What language is needed? What are the forms that induce Marduk to respond with fire instead of ignoring the mage? Does the mage know the True name of the fire spirit to reliably evoke its power? All of this needs to be researched ahead of time, which is why Hermetic mages have extensive libraries and speak several languages. It is rude to evoke a god with the wrong language on the wrong day and terrible to ignore the rituals agreed upon in a pact made in the days of Enoch that only a Hermetic, with her hours and years of study has mastered. Besides, the planets are not in the correct alignment for an evocation anyway so better to use the Latin rote for fire using transfiguration of earthly energies instead. Any first year acolyte would know this. (rolls eyes sardonically)<br /> <br /> This would work for all Traditions. A Dreamspeaker might need to bribe a fire spirit with alcohol, which would ignite when spit at a target. Knowing which spirits like liquor and which do not takes research. A Celestial might only create fire to show the power of the Divine, perhaps to banish an unpure entity that is not part of the Design. Holy prayers can make unclean vampires ignite to banish them from the realms of men, but which prayer? Research. How much study is involved in making fire from qi (ki) for an Akashic Brother? Channeling inner energy in this manner is not done lightly or without extensive practice and understanding of several underlying principles.<br /> <br /> This list goes on. The point is that the game could be geared to encourage study and to encourage use of rotes and paradigm for functional reliability as opposed to just for flavor.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that is my suggestion for this. Whether you like my secondary idea or not, I recommend tacking Prime to Arete as a freebie and using the points for something else that encourages the game you and your players want to play.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}